<title>GERMANY: German 1997 grain area put at 7.02 mln ha - ZMP.</title>
<headline>German 1997 grain area put at 7.02 mln ha - ZMP.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latest data from Germany's farm price office ZMP showed 1997 grain area at 7.02 million hectares, up four percent from 1996.</p>
<p>This was slightly below ZMP's June 19 forecast of 7.04 million ha and compared with 6.71 million ha in 1996. The figures were rounded.</p>
<p>A weekly report from ZMP detailed figures for individual crops, citing extensive surveys carried out by statistics offices in the individual German states, which included responses up to July 15.</p>
<p>The combined winter, spring and durum wheat area was 2.72 million ha versus 2.59 million in 1996. The combined winter and spring barley area was 2.28 million ha versus 2.21 million ha last year.</p>
<p>ZMP gave the following details (in ha) --</p>
<p>					  1996	     1997</p>
<p>    winter wheat		  2,543,521     2,653,325</p>
<p>    spring wheat		     42,884	  65,940</p>
<p>    durum				 8,013	   7,941</p>
<p>    rye				 809,052	 843,310</p>
<p>    winter barley		 1,413,062     1,429,217</p>
<p>    spring barley		   795,345	 846,816</p>
<p>    oats				301,888	 307,879</p>
<p>    triticale			 364,224	 433,952</p>
<p>    mixed grains		     57,265	  62,242</p>
<p>    maize for silage		277,254	 291,896</p>
<p>    corn/cob maize		   94,862	  77,374</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
